# The re-created incarnation's first initialisation seeds the floor plus one but
# claims nothing (#5668). After a new-build purge the WAL-side floor refuses a
# straddler's re-presented claim without it. After a purge that finished on 10.2.0
# the catch-up raises only the floor row: the entries stay loaded and a running WAL
# shard's in-memory floor is not raised, so a straddler of L's own shard root meets
# its loaded entry and is allocated above the recorded close. There the claim is
# what refuses it. Moved from the design's ReadPositionHonestRoutingInitWithoutClaim.
MODULE: StraddlerBelowInitRoutingInitWithoutClaim
TARGET: StraddlerBelowInit
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a re-created tree's marker reads initialised before its seeded generation is claimed
PERTURBS: FirstInit

--- FIND
    /\ entryRow' = [entryRow EXCEPT !["s"] = Max2(@, gen'["s"])]
    /\ loaded' = [loaded EXCEPT !["s"] = Max2(@, gen'["s"])]
    /\ fo' = [fo EXCEPT !["s"] = FALSE]
    /\ closedAt' = next
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the initialisation claims nothing.
    /\ entryRow' = entryRow
    /\ loaded' = loaded
    /\ UNCHANGED fo
    /\ closedAt' = next
--- END
